{"width": 612, "height": 792, "words": [{"index": 0, "str": "SHEAF: Self-profiled Hardness Estimation from Answer-set Flux", "x": 55.903, "y": 78.4096, "baseline": 95.625, "width": 500.65826279999993, "height": 17.2154, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f1"}, {"index": 1, "str": "for Predicting Query Hardness in Graph-based ANN Search", "x": 74.031, "y": 98.33459999999995, "baseline": 115.54999999999995, "width": 463.9378145999999, "height": 17.2154, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f1"}, {"index": 2, "str": "", "x": 226.207, "y": 127.63379999999994, "baseline": 139.58899999999994, "width": 0, "height": 11.9552, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 3, "str": "Dongfang Zhao (dzhao@uw.edu)", "x": 226.207, "y": 127.63379999999994, "baseline": 139.58899999999994, "width": 161.29955840000008, "height": 11.9552, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 4, "str": "", "x": 53.798, "y": 149.1349, "baseline": 160.04399999999998, "width": 0, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 5, "str": "Abstract", "x": 53.798, "y": 149.1349, "baseline": 160.04399999999998, "width": 41.61821650000001, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 6, "str": "", "x": 53.798, "y": 164.77660000000006, "baseline": 173.74300000000005, "width": 0, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 7, "str": "Graph-based approximate nearest neighbor (ANN) search is usually", "x": 53.798, "y": 164.77660000000006, "baseline": 173.74300000000005, "width": 240.4757994240001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 8, "str": "governed by a beam-width parameter that trades recall for through-", "x": 53.798, "y": 175.7356, "baseline": 184.702, "width": 241.7587119360001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 9, "str": "put and is fixed for the whole workload. Yet, queries may not be", "x": 53.798, "y": 186.69359999999998, "baseline": 195.65999999999997, "width": 240.24912883200008, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 10, "str": "equally hard: for example, on the widely used data set SIFT1M,", "x": 53.798, "y": 197.65260000000004, "baseline": 206.61900000000003, "width": 241.23686745600008, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 11, "str": "the beam that a query needs to reach 95% recall varies by more", "x": 53.798, "y": 208.61159999999998, "baseline": 217.57799999999997, "width": 240.24912883200022, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 12, "str": "than 32", "x": 53.798, "y": 219.57060000000004, "baseline": 228.53700000000003, "width": 27.8944704, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 13, "str": "×", "x": 81.692, "y": 219.57060000000004, "baseline": 228.53700000000003, "width": 5.7026304, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f5"}, {"index": 14, "str": ". Therefore, serving each query at its own width would", "x": 87.394, "y": 219.57060000000004, "baseline": 228.53700000000003, "width": 206.64772416000008, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 15, "str": "help if the system could tell, cheaply and in advance, how hard it", "x": 53.798, "y": 230.5296, "baseline": 239.49599999999998, "width": 240.24313927680006, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 16, "str": "is. The prevailing proxy for this difficulty is called local intrinsic", "x": 53.798, "y": 241.48860000000005, "baseline": 250.45500000000004, "width": 240.24912883199994, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 17, "str": "dimensionality (LID); however, LID is static and geometric, which", "x": 53.798, "y": 252.4476, "baseline": 261.414, "width": 240.24732658559995, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 18, "str": "makes it only weakly predict the minimum beam.", "x": 53.798, "y": 263.4066, "baseline": 272.37300000000005, "width": 181.59649920000012, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 19, "str": "This paper presents a new measure, namely Self-profiled Hard-", "x": 63.761, "y": 274.3656, "baseline": 283.332, "width": 231.80228688000005, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 20, "str": "ness Estimation from Answer-set Flux (SHEAF), which represents", "x": 53.798, "y": 285.3246, "baseline": 294.291, "width": 240.24908400000007, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 21, "str": "a query’s hardness as how much its own top-", "x": 53.798, "y": 296.2836, "baseline": 305.25, "width": 163.496206848, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 22, "str": "𝑘", "x": 216.934, "y": 296.2836, "baseline": 305.25, "width": 4.357670400000001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f6"}, {"index": 23, "str": " ", "x": 221.2916704, "y": 296.2836, "baseline": 305.25, "width": 2.955664568527935, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f6"}, {"index": 24, "str": "answer set changes", "x": 224.203, "y": 296.2836, "baseline": 305.25, "width": 69.84269683200002, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 25, "str": "between two shallow probe widths. We design a self-profiling esti-", "x": 53.798, "y": 307.2416, "baseline": 316.208, "width": 241.75790496000005, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 26, "str": "mator that turns this flux into a deployable per-query beam predic-", "x": 53.798, "y": 318.20059999999995, "baseline": 327.167, "width": 241.75911542400016, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 27, "str": "tor; furthermore, we develop a fixed-probe evaluation protocol that", "x": 53.798, "y": 329.15959999999995, "baseline": 338.126, "width": 240.24733555200015, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 28, "str": "scores each measure over all queries with an observed minimum", "x": 53.798, "y": 340.11859999999996, "baseline": 349.085, "width": 240.25114627199997, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 29, "str": "sufficient beam. On popular ANN indexes such as CAGRA and", "x": 53.798, "y": 351.07759999999996, "baseline": 360.044, "width": 240.24912883200005, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 30, "str": "HNSW across four diverse data sets, SHEAF predicts the per-query", "x": 53.798, "y": 362.03659999999996, "baseline": 371.003, "width": 240.47579942400006, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 31, "str": "beam better than five baseline measures on both GPU and CPU by", "x": 53.798, "y": 372.99559999999997, "baseline": 381.962, "width": 240.47617601280007, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 32, "str": "up to 1", "x": 53.798, "y": 383.95459999999997, "baseline": 392.921, "width": 25.485413913600006, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 33, "str": ".", "x": 79.425, "y": 383.95459999999997, "baseline": 392.921, "width": 1.9726080000000001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f6"}, {"index": 34, "str": "55", "x": 81.55, "y": 383.95459999999997, "baseline": 392.921, "width": 8.372107008000002, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f4"}, {"index": 35, "str": "×", "x": 89.922, "y": 383.95459999999997, "baseline": 392.921, "width": 5.7026304, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f5"}, {"index": 36, "str": " ", "x": 95.6246304, "y": 383.95459999999997, "baseline": 392.921, "width": 2.222479681274894, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f5"}, {"index": 37, "str": "in held-out correlation, using only two shallow probe", "x": 97.856, "y": 383.95459999999997, "baseline": 392.921, "width": 196.1863742208, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 38, "str": "searches and no query-time ground truth.", "x": 53.798, "y": 394.9136, "baseline": 403.88, "width": 152.85022080000007, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 39, "str": "", "x": 53.798, "y": 414.9949, "baseline": 425.904, "width": 0, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 40, "str": "Keywords", "x": 53.798, "y": 414.9949, "baseline": 425.904, "width": 49.080040900000014, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 41, "str": "", "x": 53.484, "y": 430.6366, "baseline": 439.603, "width": 0, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 42, "str": "Approximate nearest neighbor search, graph-based index, query", "x": 53.484, "y": 430.6366, "baseline": 439.603, "width": 240.7978725120001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 43, "str": "hardness estimation, local intrinsic dimensionality", "x": 53.798, "y": 441.59459999999996, "baseline": 450.561, "width": 184.4478144, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 44, "str": "", "x": 53.798, "y": 463.5619, "baseline": 474.471, "width": 0, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 45, "str": "1", "x": 53.798, "y": 463.5619, "baseline": 474.471, "width": 5.607277400000001, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 46, "str": " ", "x": 59.4052774, "y": 463.5619, "baseline": 474.471, "width": 10.909099999999995, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 47, "str": "Introduction", "x": 70.3143774, "y": 463.5619, "baseline": 474.471, "width": 63.06550710000002, "height": 10.9091, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f3"}, {"index": 48, "str": "", "x": 53.798, "y": 479.20259999999996, "baseline": 488.169, "width": 0, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 49, "str": "Graph-based approximate nearest neighbor (ANN) search is usu-", "x": 53.798, "y": 479.20259999999996, "baseline": 488.169, "width": 241.758173952, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 50, "str": "ally governed by multiple parameters; one of the most important", "x": 53.798, "y": 490.16159999999996, "baseline": 499.128, "width": 240.24437664000007, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 51, "str": "parameters is the search width, also known as the beam width. On", "x": 53.798, "y": 501.12059999999997, "baseline": 510.087, "width": 240.25065311999995, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 52, "str": "GPUs, cuVS CAGRA’s", "x": 53.798, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 82.54019520000004, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 53, "str": " ", "x": 136.33819520000003, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 2.3938047999999696, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 54, "str": "itopk_size", "x": 138.732, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 44.832000000000015, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f7"}, {"index": 55, "str": " ", "x": 183.5640000000001, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 2.345098039215571, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f7"}, {"index": 56, "str": "[37], like HNSW’s", "x": 185.956, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 67.52927244800001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 57, "str": " ", "x": 253.48527244800002, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 2.3927275519999682, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 58, "str": "ef", "x": 255.878, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 8.966400000000002, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f7"}, {"index": 59, "str": " ", "x": 264.8444, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 2.3447058823529243, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f7"}, {"index": 60, "str": "[32] on", "x": 267.236, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 26.80434566400005, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 61, "str": "the CPU, sets the beam width that trades recall for throughput. In", "x": 53.798, "y": 523.0386, "baseline": 532.005, "width": 240.24732658560004, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 62, "str": "practice, the beam width is tuned once to place the whole work-", "x": 53.798, "y": 533.9975999999999, "baseline": 542.9639999999999, "width": 241.75817395200028, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 63, "str": "load at a single point on the recall-throughput curve. However,", "x": 53.798, "y": 544.9566, "baseline": 553.923, "width": 241.23686745600028, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 64, "str": "this one-size-fits-all setting ignores the fact that many queries in", "x": 53.798, "y": 555.9156, "baseline": 564.8820000000001, "width": 240.243569664, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 65, "str": "the real-world are not equally hard. As shown in Figure 1(a), our", "x": 53.798, "y": 566.8746, "baseline": 575.841, "width": 240.41375193599998, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 66, "str": "experiments show that on CAGRA over SIFT1M [24], the minimum", "x": 53.798, "y": 577.8335999999999, "baseline": 586.8, "width": 240.246720896, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 67, "str": "", "x": 53.798, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 0, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f7"}, {"index": 68, "str": "itopk", "x": 53.798, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 22.416000000000004, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f7"}, {"index": 69, "str": " ", "x": 76.214, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 2.4000000000000075, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f7"}, {"index": 70, "str": "a query needs to reach recall@10", "x": 78.662, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 124.69285555200005, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 71, "str": " ", "x": 203.3548555520001, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 2.449144447999913, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 72, "str": "≥", "x": 205.804, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 5.7026304, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f5"}, {"index": 73, "str": " ", "x": 211.5066304, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 2.891538823529395, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f5"}, {"index": 74, "str": "0", "x": 214.456, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 4.252763520000001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f4"}, {"index": 75, "str": ".", "x": 218.853, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 1.9726080000000001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f6"}, {"index": 76, "str": "95 spans more than", "x": 220.978, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 73.065220992, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f4"}, {"index": 77, "str": "32", "x": 53.798, "y": 599.7506, "baseline": 608.717, "width": 8.455494528000001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f4"}, {"index": 78, "str": "×", "x": 62.254, "y": 599.7506, "baseline": 608.717, "width": 5.7026304, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f5"}, {"index": 79, "str": " ", "x": 67.9566304, "y": 599.7506, "baseline": 608.717, "width": 2.2025341222879717, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f5"}, {"index": 80, "str": "with 61% of queries satisfied at the smallest beam and a long", "x": 70.19, "y": 599.7506, "baseline": 608.717, "width": 223.8523986816001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 81, "str": "tail needing an order of magnitude more. Therefore, serving each", "x": 53.798, "y": 610.7095999999999, "baseline": 619.6759999999999, "width": 240.2439641856002, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 82, "str": "query at its own width, i.e., small for the easy majority and large", "x": 53.798, "y": 621.6686, "baseline": 630.635, "width": 240.24466356479996, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 83, "str": "only for the hard tail, would move the system off that uniform curve.", "x": 53.798, "y": 632.6276, "baseline": 641.594, "width": 241.62690585600004, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 84, "str": "Doing so rests on one ingredient above all: a way to tell, cheaply", "x": 53.798, "y": 643.5866, "baseline": 652.553, "width": 240.4777720320001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 85, "str": "and before committing the search budget, how hard each query is.", "x": 53.798, "y": 654.5455999999999, "baseline": 663.512, "width": 241.62576712320003, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 86, "str": "One prevailing way to price a query is the so-called local intrin-", "x": 63.761, "y": 665.5046, "baseline": 674.471, "width": 231.79944453120004, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 87, "str": "sic dimensionality (LID) [2, 19], which is a static geometric measure", "x": 53.798, "y": 676.4636, "baseline": 685.4300000000001, "width": 240.2507719680001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 88, "str": "for grading a query’s difficulty [4]. However, recent studies showed", "x": 53.798, "y": 687.4226, "baseline": 696.389, "width": 240.24592057600006, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 89, "str": "that LID-based approaches exhibit two limitations. First, LID is a", "x": 53.798, "y": 698.3806, "baseline": 707.347, "width": 240.2435696640001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 90, "str": "16", "x": 357.57934286506844, "y": 239.93222604311237, "baseline": 246.69275604311235, "width": 8.598922582851484, "height": 6.76053, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f8"}, {"index": 91, "str": " ", "x": 366.1782654479199, "y": 239.93222604311237, "baseline": 246.69275604311235, "width": 5.211168244150096, "height": 6.76053, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f8"}, {"index": 92, "str": "32", "x": 371.2111596264376, "y": 239.93222604311237, "baseline": 246.69275604311235, "width": 8.598922582851484, "height": 6.76053, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f8"}, {"index": 93, "str": " ", "x": 379.8100822092891, "y": 239.93222604311237, "baseline": 246.69275604311235, "width": 5.211168244150156, "height": 6.76053, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f8"}, {"index": 94, "str": "96 192 384", "x": 384.84297638780686, "y":