"}, {"index": 146, "str": "quence [1, 28], but they do not directly correlate the stability of", "x": 317.955, "y": 413.4496, "baseline": 422.416, "width": 240.243554432, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 147, "str": "the top-", "x": 317.955, "y": 424.4086, "baseline": 433.375, "width": 28.355881344000004, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 148, "str": "𝑘", "x": 345.95, "y": 424.4086, "baseline": 433.375, "width": 4.357670400000001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f6"}, {"index": 149, "str": " ", "x": 350.3076704, "y": 424.4086, "baseline": 433.375, "width": 2.919724081632629, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f6"}, {"index": 150, "str": "answer set itself, which is a direct indicator of how much", "x": 353.169, "y": 424.4086, "baseline": 433.375, "width": 205.02875097600003, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 151, "str": "more work a query needs. What is desired is a cheap, online, ground-", "x": 317.955, "y": 435.3676, "baseline": 444.334, "width": 241.75871193600003, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 152, "str": "truth-free measure that actually quantifies a query’s graph-search", "x": 317.955, "y": 446.3266, "baseline": 455.293, "width": 240.24923642880015, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 153, "str": "cost, i.e., beam width.", "x": 317.955, "y": 457.2856, "baseline": 466.252, "width": 78.6442944, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 154, "str": "Our insight toward this goal is that a query’s hardness is not only", "x": 327.918, "y": 468.24359999999996, "baseline": 477.21, "width": 230.52004684800002, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 155, "str": "geometric but algorithmic: a query is hard exactly when its own", "x": 317.955, "y": 479.20259999999996, "baseline": 488.169, "width": 240.24912883199997, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 156, "str": "search has not yet settled, and more importantly, that state is already", "x": 317.955, "y": 490.16159999999996, "baseline": 499.128, "width": 240.47579942400012, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 157, "str": "visible in the search’s early behavior without ground truth at query", "x": 317.731, "y": 501.12059999999997, "baseline": 510.087, "width": 240.70426329600002, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 158, "str": "time. We formulate it as", "x": 317.955, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 86.10451852800003, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 159, "str": " ", "x": 404.0595185279998, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 2.2953984000000163, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 160, "str": "answer-set flux", "x": 406.3090089599998, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 52.810302720000024, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f10"}, {"index": 161, "str": ", how much a query’s top-", "x": 459.1193116799999, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 94.40830156800014, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 162, "str": "𝑘", "x": 553.167, "y": 512.0796, "baseline": 521.046, "width": 4.357670400000001, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f6"}, {"index": 163, "str": "", "x": 317.955, "y": 523.0386, "baseline": 532.005, "width": 0, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 164, "str": "result changes between two shallow probe widths. A query whose", "x": 317.955, "y": 523.0386, "baseline": 532.005, "width": 240.24561400320002, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 165, "str": "answer set is still churning is far from settled; one whose answer set", "x": 317.955, "y": 533.9975999999999, "baseline": 542.9639999999999, "width": 240.24733555200015, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 166, "str": "has stopped moving, and whose distances have stopped tightening,", "x": 317.955, "y": 544.9566, "baseline": 553.923, "width": 241.23148761600015, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 167, "str": "is a candidate for convergence that the estimator then confirms.", "x": 317.955, "y": 555.9156, "baseline": 564.8820000000001, "width": 241.63013376000035, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 168, "str": "Performance-wise, this flux is computed solely from the results of", "x": 317.955, "y": 566.8746, "baseline": 575.841, "width": 240.2473265856, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 169, "str": "two shallow probe searches without ground truth or access to the", "x": 317.955, "y": 577.8335999999999, "baseline": 586.8, "width": 240.24572160000008, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 170, "str": "graph index.", "x": 317.955, "y": 588.7916, "baseline": 597.758, "width": 45.77347199999998, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 171, "str": "This paper turns the above insight into a new quantitative mea-", "x": 327.918, "y": 599.7506, "baseline": 608.717, "width": 231.80131850880016, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 172, "str": "sure, namely Self-profiled Hardness Estimation from Answer-set", "x": 317.955, "y": 610.7095999999999, "baseline": 619.6759999999999, "width": 240.24356966399992, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 173, "str": "Flux (SHEAF). What SHEAF contributes is a query-hardness mea-", "x": 317.955, "y": 621.6686, "baseline": 630.635, "width": 241.7578690944, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 174, "str": "sure and the machinery to read and evaluate it: flux itself, a self-", "x": 317.955, "y": 632.6276, "baseline": 641.594, "width": 241.75817395200028, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 175, "str": "profiling estimator that turns it into a per-query cost prediction, and", "x": 317.955, "y": 643.5866, "baseline": 652.553, "width": 240.24733555200004, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 176, "str": "a protocol that scores that prediction with a probe held below the", "x": 317.955, "y": 654.5455999999999, "baseline": 663.512, "width": 240.2500434048003, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 177, "str": "hard tail’s cost. An adaptive serving policy is the application such", "x": 317.955, "y": 665.5046, "baseline": 674.471, "width": 240.24732658559995, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 178, "str": "a measure feeds; how accurately the measure predicts per-query", "x": 317.955, "y": 676.4636, "baseline": 685.4300000000001, "width": 240.47777203200016, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 179, "str": "cost, which is what we study here, is what any such policy would", "x": 317.955, "y": 687.4226, "baseline": 696.389, "width": 240.2469948287999, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 180, "str": "rest on. In summary, this paper makes the following contributions.", "x": 317.955, "y": 698.3806, "baseline": 707.347, "width": 241.62898606080017, "height": 8.9664, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 181, "str": "", "x": 304.298, "y": 712.3292, "baseline": 719.303, "width": 0, "height": 6.9738, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 182, "str": "1", "x": 304.298, "y": 712.3292, "baseline": 719.303, "width": 3.2428169999999996, "height": 6.9738, "angle": 0, "font": "g_d0_f2"}, {"index": 183, "str": "arXiv:2607.12229v1 [cs.IR] 14 Jul 2026", "x": 36, "y": 614.8, "baseline": 634.8, "width": 334.41999999999996, "height": 20, "angle": -1.5707963267948966, "font": "g_d0_f11"}]}